  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 121912,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/ilwren/hcvault",
  "published": "2026-10-16T13:39:15.2Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.6.3: streaming file access - OpenFile(path, VcFileMode.Read/Create/Append) returns a Stream with random-position reads, in-place writes, zero-filled holes and appends in constant memory (FAT implements a managed cluster-chain stream, exFAT is backed by the native file API). In-place exFAT re-formatting (VolumeFilesystem.FormatExFat). Opening with an explicit KDF (VolumeOpenOptions.Kdf) skips the try-every-KDF search, so wrong credentials fail after a single derivation. Fixed: exFAT operations were not safe across concurrently used volumes (FatFs resolves unprefixed paths against a process-global current drive - operations could land on the wrong mount); every call is now pinned to its own volume. Fixed: ContainerSize.GetRequiredContainerSize returned FAT containers the creator then rejected (the floors are the exact native minimums now).",
